# Local width-measurement tool. Kept out of the repo deliberately: it puts the
# terminal in raw mode and reads cursor-position replies to measure what a glyph
# really costs, which is how the width profiles were derived and how to check
# them against a terminal that disagrees. Useful when a board looks skewed;
# not something a task tracker should carry a subcommand for.
#   go run ./tools/doctor          # or --json
tools/
